WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.570
I typed just this to the

2
00:00:02.570 --> 00:00:05.050
agent: yes, send it.

3
00:00:05.670 --> 00:00:08.110
Nobody had asked me anything.

4
00:00:09.020 --> 00:00:12.320
It made up a message, and sent it!

5
00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:15.330
Wasn’t it trained to ask first?

6
00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:18.380
Today: permissions and

7
00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:20.240
approval, checked in code.

8
00:00:21.470 --> 00:00:23.670
Every tool gets a permission level.

9
00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:26.980
Read only: it may look things

10
00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:28.080
up, like the weather.

11
00:00:28.710 --> 00:00:31.590
Ask first: it waits for a person’s

12
00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:33.750
yes, like a message to parents.

13
00:00:34.540 --> 00:00:37.080
Allowed: it acts freely, for

14
00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:38.240
low-risk jobs only.

15
00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:42.060
Darsi Tiny learned to ask before sending.

16
00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:45.050
But learned behaviour can fail.

17
00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:48.300
Requests it should refuse, worded in

18
00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:50.540
new ways, still got a tool call

19
00:00:50.540 --> 00:00:52.220
twenty-eight percent of the time in

20
00:00:52.220 --> 00:00:54.140
English, and twelve percent in Arabic.

21
00:00:54.880 --> 00:00:57.680
A promise to ask is not a lock.

22
00:00:58.970 --> 00:01:00.470
So the check belongs in

23
00:01:00.470 --> 00:01:02.110
code, outside the model.

24
00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:06.300
Before any action runs, the app asks: did

25
00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:08.980
the model ask this person about this exact

26
00:01:08.980 --> 00:01:11.360
action, and did they say yes?

27
00:01:12.070 --> 00:01:13.930
If not, the call is blocked,

28
00:01:14.370 --> 00:01:15.290
however it’s worded.

29
00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:18.140
Here’s that check in code.

30
00:01:18.740 --> 00:01:22.520
It looks up the tool’s level, and a tool

31
00:01:22.520 --> 00:01:25.080
missing from the table counts as off.

32
00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:27.440
Allowed tools run.

33
00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:31.200
Ask-first tools run only after a yes.

34
00:01:31.890 --> 00:01:33.370
Everything else is blocked.

35
00:01:34.700 --> 00:01:36.900
Every action also goes in a log:

36
00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:39.320
what was asked, the exact call,

37
00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:41.220
who approved it and when.

38
00:01:41.810 --> 00:01:43.410
When a parent asks about a

39
00:01:43.410 --> 00:01:45.310
message, the log answers.

40
00:01:46.090 --> 00:01:48.410
Blocked calls go in too: they

41
00:01:48.410 --> 00:01:49.670
show where the agent slips.

42
00:01:51.170 --> 00:01:51.650
Quick check!

43
00:01:52.260 --> 00:01:56.000
Darsi Tiny learned to ask before sending.

44
00:01:56.670 --> 00:01:59.750
Why check the approval in code as well?

45
00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:03.240
Because learned behaviour can fail.

46
00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:06.500
New wordings slip past it, and on

47
00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:08.600
its own, yes, send it made the

48
00:02:08.600 --> 00:02:10.040
model invent a message.

49
00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:13.370
The code check doesn’t guess: no yes

50
00:02:13.370 --> 00:02:16.050
to this exact action, no action.

51
00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:18.460
Now look at this code.

52
00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:21.020
When the model asks to send a

53
00:02:21.020 --> 00:02:23.420
message, the app just sends it.

54
00:02:24.020 --> 00:02:25.620
Nothing checks that a person

55
00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:28.780
said yes, so one slip becomes a

56
00:02:28.780 --> 00:02:30.540
message to every parent.

57
00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:34.280
In the app, send the message to Mrs

58
00:02:34.280 --> 00:02:37.880
Mensah: it asks first, so say no, then

59
00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:38.200
yes.

60
00:02:38.870 --> 00:02:41.490
Then switch the code check off, choose

61
00:02:41.490 --> 00:02:44.730
Allowed, and send yes, send it on its own.

62
00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:47.520
Switch the check on and try again.

63
00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:49.490
Your turn.

64
00:02:50.130 --> 00:02:52.430
The agent wants to send the

65
00:02:52.430 --> 00:02:54.710
fees letter to all parents.

66
00:02:55.640 --> 00:02:57.580
What must happen first?

67
00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:01.440
A named person reads the exact

68
00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:03.200
message and says yes.

69
00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:06.100
Remember: every tool gets

70
00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:07.040
a permission level.

71
00:03:07.670 --> 00:03:09.550
Approval is checked in code,

72
00:03:09.910 --> 00:03:11.470
never only by the model.

73
00:03:12.070 --> 00:03:13.450
And every action is

74
00:03:13.450 --> 00:03:15.190
logged, blocked ones too.

75
00:03:16.380 --> 00:03:17.700
Try it in class tomorrow:

76
00:03:18.040 --> 00:03:19.420
run an approval drill.

77
00:03:20.010 --> 00:03:21.930
One pupil is the agent and

78
00:03:21.930 --> 00:03:23.210
hands over action cards.

79
00:03:23.960 --> 00:03:26.160
Another is the code check, with the

80
00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:28.560
permissions table, and blocks any

81
00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:30.700
action card without a signed yes.
